1
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:34,990
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,890
[Episode 9]

3
00:01:38,310 --> 00:01:39,310
We're here, miss.

4
00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:40,720
Careful.

5
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,330
Miss, that's 2 yuan.

6
00:01:43,759 --> 00:01:45,020
I don't have any money.

7
00:01:45,150 --> 00:01:45,950
Come on, miss.

8
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,509
I pulled you all this way.

9
00:01:47,509 --> 00:01:49,090
How can you not pay?

10
00:01:49,110 --> 00:01:50,390
I just don't have any.

11
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:51,590
You just got back?

12
00:01:53,759 --> 00:01:54,490
He has money.

13
00:01:54,759 --> 00:01:55,640
Ask him for it.

14
00:01:56,710 --> 00:01:57,030
Here.

15
00:01:57,030 --> 00:01:57,960
He owes me money.

16
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:58,920
Thank you.

17
00:01:59,039 --> 00:01:59,870
Alright, as long as someone pays.

18
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:01,070
Why did you drink that much?

19
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:03,000
Xin Xiang! Xin Xiang!

20
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,420
What are you doing? Come here.

21
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:06,360
Boss.

22
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,960
Why did she drink so much?

23
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:10,750
Where did you go?

24
00:02:12,030 --> 00:02:14,290
Young Master Feng didn't give you a ride?

25
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:16,840
I just went to Qibao Town in Songjiang.

26
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,370
I didn't take him with me.

27
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:20,690
How come you've started gambling now?

28
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,590
Don't you want to save people?

29
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:24,630
Do you think saving people
doesn't cost money?

30
00:02:24,630 --> 00:02:26,960
One after another, people come
begging me for help.

31
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:29,160
Do they think any of that comes for free?

32
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,180
But can you even win any money?

33
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:34,000
You lost so badly you didn't even
have enough left for a rickshaw ride.

34
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,079
Who do you think you're looking down on?

35
00:02:36,079 --> 00:02:37,680
Next time you go to Qibao Town,

36
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,800
remember to take me along.

37
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:41,150
I'm even better at rolling dice
than taking pictures.

38
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:41,910
Get lost.

39
00:02:48,190 --> 00:02:49,079
Chen.

40
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,120
Aren't you annoying?

41
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:54,680
You have to meddle in everyone's business.

42
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:56,800
You,

43
00:02:58,470 --> 00:02:59,190
come here.

44
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:02,110
Let me show you something great.

45
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,560
Alright, take it.

46
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:18,710
Take it.

47
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:21,310
It's all yours.

48
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:24,680
What do I need this for?

49
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:27,079
To save your beloved cousin.

50
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:29,520
In this world,

51
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:32,870
you can't do anything without money.

52
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:34,730
Good thing you met me.

53
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,360
I told you already,

54
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,300
I don't need you to help me like this.

55
00:03:40,829 --> 00:03:42,690
I'll never be able to pay you back.

56
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:47,590
I'd rather you owe me

57
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,190
than ignore me.

58
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:56,510
And I definitely don't want you
to be unhappy.

59
00:04:00,170 --> 00:04:01,630
Money is nothing.

60
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:03,610
I can't care about it less.

61
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,360
Money isn't nothing.

62
00:04:12,150 --> 00:04:13,400
I'm indebted to you.

63
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:15,750
I think

64
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,800
you're one of

65
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,459
the best people in this world.

66
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:24,140
Whoever it is you're trying to save,

67
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:26,070
whatever their identity,

68
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:27,560
I'll support you.

69
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:38,330
Now there's no way to save her
even if I want to.

70
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:42,070
Where there's money, there's a way.

71
00:04:43,159 --> 00:04:44,950
If only it were that simple.

72
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,690
Then what else can I do to help you?

73
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,670
Before I change my mind,

74
00:04:54,390 --> 00:04:55,520
hurry up and tell me.

75
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:00,530
How about you teach me how to dance?

76
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:03,670
Why do you want to learn to dance?

77
00:05:05,070 --> 00:05:06,310
If I can dance,

78
00:05:07,630 --> 00:05:08,950
maybe I can save her.

79
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:14,200
Dancing's my specialty.

80
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,160
Come here.

81
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:26,790
Put your arm around my waist.

82
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:29,950
Let's go.

83
00:05:56,270 --> 00:05:58,150
[Newsstand]

84
00:06:01,070 --> 00:06:02,610
Newspapers for sale! Newspapers for sale!

85
00:06:02,610 --> 00:06:04,180
-Want to buy cigarettes?
-Come check it out.

86
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:05,060
Newspapers.

87
00:06:10,630 --> 00:06:12,230
Want to buy cigarettes, sir?

88
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:25,570
Here.

89
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:30,890
I was worried it might draw attention,

90
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:32,070
so I bought a few different kinds.

91
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:33,800
It looks more natural that way.

92
00:06:34,990 --> 00:06:35,750
Smart.

93
00:06:38,550 --> 00:06:44,880
[Missing Person Notice]

94
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:10,180
Well, I'll head back now.

95
00:07:11,630 --> 00:07:13,430
You don't have to come every day.

96
00:07:13,890 --> 00:07:15,420
It might arouse suspicion.

97
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:18,310
I'll come back after closing tonight.

98
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:19,770
If you don't get back soon,

99
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:22,880
the photo studio will have to
shut down for good.

100
00:07:23,870 --> 00:07:24,470
I'm off.

101
00:07:34,510 --> 00:07:35,780
Any big news?

102
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:40,560
A female Communist at Renji Hospital
was abducted,

103
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:43,159
and the Labor Union's protest
has died down.

104
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:47,230
Does that count as big news?

105
00:07:49,550 --> 00:07:51,590
They've passed judgment on you.

106
00:07:57,190 --> 00:07:59,790
Last time, you said you could
send me to Yan'an.

107
00:08:02,430 --> 00:08:04,890
There's no place for me
in Shanghai anymore.

108
00:08:06,550 --> 00:08:07,680
I've made up my mind.

109
00:08:09,110 --> 00:08:10,070
I can go there.

110
00:08:11,970 --> 00:08:12,940
At least there,

111
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:15,100
no one will try to kill me.

112
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:19,190
Are you sure?

113
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,890
Alright, I'll make the arrangements.

114
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:29,430
Thank you.

115
00:08:40,510 --> 00:08:41,220
Comrade,

116
00:08:42,110 --> 00:08:43,169
let's shake hands.

117
00:08:47,950 --> 00:08:49,340
Have a safe trip.

118
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:55,500
Let's go.

119
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:16,070
Where is she?

120
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:19,760
Where's my cousin?

121
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:22,420
She just left.

122
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:26,570
The higher-ups sent someone
to take her away.

123
00:09:28,430 --> 00:09:29,890
Why didn't she wait for me?

124
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,500
It was the higher-ups' decision.

125
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:37,230
She needed to be transferred
as soon as possible.

126
00:09:37,790 --> 00:09:39,790
You should have told me beforehand.

127
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:42,620
I'm Shen Kexi's family, after all.

128
00:09:54,340 --> 00:09:56,140
Did she leave any message for me?

129
00:09:58,150 --> 00:09:59,270
She said

130
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:03,190
you might meet again someday.

131
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:08,110
How could we possibly meet?

132
00:10:09,270 --> 00:10:10,470
She's gone to Yan'an,

133
00:10:10,570 --> 00:10:11,700
and I'm in Shanghai.

134
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:14,630
We're in two different worlds now.

135
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:18,190
So stop telling others

136
00:10:18,190 --> 00:10:19,650
about your relationship.

137
00:10:25,550 --> 00:10:26,700
Tell me the truth.

138
00:10:27,430 --> 00:10:28,490
Is she really safe?

139
00:10:30,550 --> 00:10:31,270
Kailai.

140
00:10:32,390 --> 00:10:34,790
Just keep the past
buried deep in your heart

141
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:36,430
and look ahead.

142
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:42,430
I'll say the same thing I said before:

143
00:10:42,430 --> 00:10:45,430
in Shanghai, it's important
to have the right mentor.

144
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:47,230
You have to trust me.

145
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:17,220
Come on. Here.

146
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:31,340
The phone.

147
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:40,100
Director.

148
00:12:40,790 --> 00:12:43,500
I saw Su Men dancing with
Detective Hua Liang.

149
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:47,390
She's gotten cozy with
the French Concession crowd too?

150
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:49,480
Yeah, that woman's got some skills.

151
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:55,140
You don't think she can actually
find that female Communist, do you?

152
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:56,910
If she really can pull that off,

153
00:12:57,950 --> 00:12:59,410
I'll take my hat off to her.

154
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:11,380
Miss Shen, you're awake.

155
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,910
The painkillers may have

156
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:17,430
made you sleep for so long
as a side effect.

157
00:13:19,030 --> 00:13:19,860
Who are you?

158
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:23,670
His name is Wang Minzhi.

159
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:25,670
And I'm his wife, Liu Qing.

160
00:13:29,390 --> 00:13:30,450
Where are we going?

161
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:38,220
Since you've been exposed,

162
00:13:38,220 --> 00:13:40,550
it's not safe to stay in Shanghai anymore.

163
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:43,820
Come with us to our station
in southern Jiangsu first.

164
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:46,040
Once we get there, if you are willing,

165
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:48,160
we'll arrange for you to go to Yan'an.

166
00:13:53,270 --> 00:13:54,400
I'm not a Communist.

167
00:13:59,150 --> 00:14:00,750
Whatever your affiliation,

168
00:14:01,070 --> 00:14:03,620
it's no small feat to survive

169
00:14:03,790 --> 00:14:04,990
such brutal torture.

170
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:07,760
Seeing the wounds on your feet

171
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:08,720
breaks my heart.

172
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:13,450
These have been difficult times

173
00:14:13,450 --> 00:14:14,380
for everyone.

174
00:14:15,510 --> 00:14:17,970
There's been a traitor
in the organization.

175
00:14:17,990 --> 00:14:21,190
The "Sparrow" operation in Shanghai
nearly got exposed.

176
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:23,060
The Hangzhou station

177
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:26,420
has been exposed by the traitor.

178
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:30,220
The intelligence networks
in southern Jiangsu and northern Zhejiang

179
00:14:30,220 --> 00:14:31,820
have completely collapsed.

180
00:14:32,150 --> 00:14:33,880
It hasn't been easy for any of us

181
00:14:33,910 --> 00:14:34,970
to make it this far.

182
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:40,920
How could this be?

183
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:46,150
Everyone's been

184
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:48,170
exceptionally cautious lately,

185
00:14:48,170 --> 00:14:49,630
including your superior.

186
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:53,690
After asking the Shanghai action team
to rescue you,

187
00:14:54,030 --> 00:14:55,960
your superior cut off all contact.

188
00:14:58,220 --> 00:15:00,620
The situation in Shanghai is complicated.

189
00:15:00,790 --> 00:15:02,190
For your safety,

190
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:05,380
we have no choice
but to evacuate you first.

191
00:15:07,790 --> 00:15:08,920
You've got it wrong.

192
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:11,700
Brother Du

193
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:14,440
may not have explained things clearly.

194
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:17,030
I'm not a Communist,

195
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:18,920
nor do I have any superior.

196
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:23,090
I'm just trying to save my own life.

197
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:25,760
It doesn't matter.

198
00:15:26,030 --> 00:15:27,580
Once we reach the liberated area,

199
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:28,840
we'll all be comrades.

200
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:34,120
Are we leaving Shanghai?

201
00:15:37,790 --> 00:15:39,590
We still have some driving to do.

202
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:46,580
Su Causeway must,
before the 27th of this month,

203
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:49,020
arrive at Jinshanzui Fishing Village.

204
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:51,430
Miss Shen,

205
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:55,700
is there anything in Shanghai
you can't bear to leave behind?

206
00:15:59,530 --> 00:16:00,990
Before we leave Shanghai,

207
00:16:02,950 --> 00:16:04,150
I need to see someone.

208
00:16:05,550 --> 00:16:06,270
Who?

209
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,900
Someone I absolutely have to see.

210
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:12,710
You should have told us sooner.

211
00:16:13,150 --> 00:16:15,080
It's very risky to stay in Shanghai

212
00:16:15,430 --> 00:16:16,340
any longer.

213
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:19,100
You should understand

214
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:20,550
how important this is.

215
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:25,620
Where is it?

216
00:16:26,150 --> 00:16:27,270
We need to hurry.

217
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:32,800
Jinshanzui

218
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:35,620
Fishing Village.

219
00:16:43,090 --> 00:16:43,800
Boss.

220
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:46,520
You've been reading this newspaper
for a while.

221
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:47,910
Is there any major news?

222
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:51,590
Today at Fairy Bath,

223
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:53,430
did anything special happen?

224
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:57,670
I actually have no idea.

225
00:17:04,650 --> 00:17:07,770
Why did she leave without saying a word?

226
00:17:13,930 --> 00:17:17,960
[Jinshanzui Fishing Village]

227
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,400
Where are we?

228
00:18:14,530 --> 00:18:16,590
This is one of our secret safe houses.

229
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:17,980
We've been driving north

230
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:19,430
this whole time.

231
00:18:20,110 --> 00:18:22,770
The Jinshanzui Fishing Village
you want to go to

232
00:18:22,830 --> 00:18:23,690
is to the south.

233
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:25,150
It's still a bit far.

234
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:26,870
Let's take a break here

235
00:18:26,870 --> 00:18:27,870
for a bit.

236
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:29,360
I'll carry you down first.

237
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:41,560
Since you're injured,

238
00:18:41,630 --> 00:18:43,090
we dare not drive too fast.

239
00:18:44,110 --> 00:18:44,830
I'm okay.

240
00:18:45,530 --> 00:18:46,730
Rest here for a while.

241
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:49,320
I'll go get something to eat from the car.

242
00:19:02,070 --> 00:19:03,930
I'll get you a bowl of water first.

243
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:14,430
What is it?

244
00:19:14,950 --> 00:19:16,550
Special Commissioner No. 1 called.

245
00:19:16,550 --> 00:19:17,150
Go ahead.

246
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:19,300
Today at Jinshanzui Fishing Village,

247
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:21,430
there will be a Communist rendezvous.

248
00:19:22,180 --> 00:19:23,900
Wake up Bi Zhongliang
of the Operations Division

249
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:25,510
and send people over immediately.
Be quick.

250
00:19:25,510 --> 00:19:26,110
Yes.

251
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:36,940
Hurry up, everyone! Hurry up!

252
00:19:38,650 --> 00:19:40,210
Hurry up! Move!

253
00:19:40,890 --> 00:19:42,300
Hurry up! Come on!

254
00:19:45,590 --> 00:19:47,590
Get in the trucks quickly! Let's go!

255
00:20:10,350 --> 00:20:12,050
Li Moqun assigned a special mission.

256
00:20:12,050 --> 00:20:13,780
He didn't specify the details.

257
00:20:15,630 --> 00:20:17,150
I have a bad feeling—

258
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,830
something's happened to Su Causeway.

259
00:20:20,070 --> 00:20:21,270
Drive to Jinshanzui.

260
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:22,710
You must get there before they do

261
00:20:22,710 --> 00:20:24,220
and notify Uncle Hai and the others
to leave.

262
00:20:24,220 --> 00:20:24,670
Got it.

263
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:52,640
Mr. Wang has been gone for so long.

264
00:20:53,510 --> 00:20:54,910
Should we go check on him?

265
00:20:55,190 --> 00:20:56,450
He should be back soon.

266
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:59,760
Here, have some warm water
to warm yourself up.

267
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:01,990
Mrs. Wang.

268
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:05,740
I feel so cold.

269
00:21:06,630 --> 00:21:07,430
You feel cold?

270
00:21:09,590 --> 00:21:10,260
Here.

271
00:21:11,060 --> 00:21:11,980
Put this on.

272
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:14,180
Take my jacket.

273
00:23:00,870 --> 00:23:03,830
You're an admirable young lady.

274
00:23:06,060 --> 00:23:07,390
But my orders are clear:

275
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:10,200
once you tell us where the rendezvous is,

276
00:23:10,460 --> 00:23:11,910
I can send you on your way.

277
00:23:16,370 --> 00:23:17,160
What a pity.

278
00:23:47,460 --> 00:23:48,610
They just left.

279
00:23:49,740 --> 00:23:50,300
Let's go!

280
00:24:15,300 --> 00:24:16,700
Any news on Su Causeway?

281
00:24:17,460 --> 00:24:18,060
Not yet.

282
00:24:28,030 --> 00:24:29,510
I only received word

283
00:24:30,020 --> 00:24:32,700
to round up a few men

284
00:24:32,910 --> 00:24:35,780
and break a female Communist prisoner
out of the hospital.

285
00:24:35,780 --> 00:24:36,780
Who sent you?

286
00:24:38,780 --> 00:24:39,980
It was Chief Cleaner.

287
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:44,500
He promised

288
00:24:45,060 --> 00:24:46,390
that once the job was done,

289
00:24:46,390 --> 00:24:48,540
he'd get all of us into No. 76.

290
00:24:50,540 --> 00:24:51,910
This Cleaner—

291
00:24:52,980 --> 00:24:56,110
I remember he's Director Li's
right-hand man, isn't he?

292
00:24:59,740 --> 00:25:01,800
Your own people broke a fugitive out,

293
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:03,960
and then pinned the blame on me—

294
00:25:05,430 --> 00:25:07,960
Director Li, do you want me dead
or something?

295
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:10,410
Inspector Su, you misunderstood.

296
00:25:11,460 --> 00:25:13,950
This was actually a setup by Cleaner.

297
00:25:14,550 --> 00:25:15,460
What trap?

298
00:25:23,270 --> 00:25:24,660
Take him away first.

299
00:25:31,110 --> 00:25:31,630
Sir!

300
00:25:32,540 --> 00:25:33,220
Sir!

301
00:25:33,470 --> 00:25:35,520
I was just following orders, sir!

302
00:25:39,300 --> 00:25:39,980
General.

303
00:25:41,950 --> 00:25:43,880
I only found out a couple of days ago

304
00:25:43,910 --> 00:25:46,740
that Cleaner, in order to confirm
Shen Kexi's affiliation

305
00:25:46,740 --> 00:25:49,260
and get useful information out of her
as quickly as possible,

306
00:25:49,260 --> 00:25:52,260
disguised himself as a Communist
and staged her rescue.

307
00:25:52,260 --> 00:25:54,910
I'm sorry you were caught
in the crossfire, Inspector Su.

308
00:25:54,910 --> 00:25:56,640
It was an unfortunate mistake.

309
00:25:57,830 --> 00:25:59,230
An unfortunate mistake?

310
00:26:00,750 --> 00:26:02,480
If I hadn't managed to find him,

311
00:26:03,740 --> 00:26:04,500
I'd probably

312
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:06,450
be on my way back to Nanjing by now,

313
00:26:08,060 --> 00:26:09,860
with this whole mess pinned on me

314
00:26:10,350 --> 00:26:11,810
and no way to clear my name.

315
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:16,260
Inspector Su, you've been wronged.

316
00:26:22,020 --> 00:26:25,740
I'd like to apologize to you
on Cleaner's behalf.

317
00:26:26,830 --> 00:26:30,490
Everything No. 76 does is for the sake of
gathering intelligence.

318
00:26:30,830 --> 00:26:32,750
Inspector Su, we ask for
your understanding

319
00:26:32,750 --> 00:26:35,280
regarding the unintended harm
caused to you.

320
00:26:37,250 --> 00:26:39,910
Did you really not know about this,
Director Li?

321
00:26:39,980 --> 00:26:40,630
I didn't.

322
00:26:44,320 --> 00:26:47,580
Your trusted man went behind your back
and acted on his own.

323
00:26:49,430 --> 00:26:51,690
I don't see any reason to keep him around.

324
00:26:52,790 --> 00:26:54,070
Although Cleaner

325
00:26:54,090 --> 00:26:55,720
handled this matter poorly,

326
00:26:56,430 --> 00:26:59,160
his competence and loyalty
are beyond question.

327
00:26:59,980 --> 00:27:01,190
Through this operation,

328
00:27:01,190 --> 00:27:02,590
Cleaner confirmed

329
00:27:02,590 --> 00:27:04,220
that Shen Kexi is a Communist.

330
00:27:04,220 --> 00:27:05,150
At the same time,

331
00:27:05,350 --> 00:27:06,630
we discovered

332
00:27:06,910 --> 00:27:08,980
a secret Communist Party hideout

333
00:27:09,540 --> 00:27:11,340
in Jinshanzui Fishing Village.

334
00:27:14,190 --> 00:27:15,390
Did you catch anyone?

335
00:27:16,500 --> 00:27:18,300
Unfortunately, we got there
a bit too late.

336
00:27:18,300 --> 00:27:19,700
The Communists got away.

337
00:27:22,310 --> 00:27:23,510
What about Shen Kexi?

338
00:27:23,950 --> 00:27:25,480
She was shot dead by our men.

339
00:27:28,900 --> 00:27:30,250
So after all that,

340
00:27:30,520 --> 00:27:32,720
we didn't get any useful intelligence.

341
00:27:34,300 --> 00:27:36,430
Apart from framing me,

342
00:27:37,140 --> 00:27:39,200
this Cleaner hasn't been of much use.

343
00:27:41,430 --> 00:27:42,690
He failed in his duties

344
00:27:43,500 --> 00:27:45,100
and deserves to be punished.

345
00:27:45,690 --> 00:27:46,380
General.

346
00:27:47,630 --> 00:27:48,980
I received word today

347
00:27:50,070 --> 00:27:51,700
that Cleaner has discovered

348
00:27:51,730 --> 00:27:55,110
that those who assassinated Dr. Hoshino
at the racecourse were NBIS agents.

349
00:27:55,110 --> 00:27:57,840
Please give him a chance
to atone for his mistake.

350
00:27:58,300 --> 00:28:00,590
Shen Kexi is just a small fry.

351
00:28:01,430 --> 00:28:03,460
The intelligence Cleaner has gathered

352
00:28:03,460 --> 00:28:04,580
is enough to wipe out

353
00:28:04,580 --> 00:28:06,840
the entire NBIS spy network in Shanghai.

354
00:28:06,980 --> 00:28:08,540
The heads of all 12 stations

355
00:28:08,940 --> 00:28:10,200
will show themselves.

356
00:28:12,390 --> 00:28:13,220
Really?

357
00:28:13,910 --> 00:28:15,910
The operation is already underway.

358
00:28:28,950 --> 00:28:30,400
Care for a song, sir?

359
00:28:30,870 --> 00:28:32,260
Care for a song, miss?

360
00:28:38,150 --> 00:28:40,600
You're making a fortune today, Auntie.

361
00:28:40,780 --> 00:28:42,460
Business is booming.

362
00:28:43,610 --> 00:28:45,570
You're such a sweet talker now.

363
00:28:46,060 --> 00:28:47,720
I'm starting to like you a bit.

364
00:28:50,120 --> 00:28:51,650
You'd better hurry up then.

365
00:28:52,430 --> 00:28:53,700
Life is short.

366
00:28:54,150 --> 00:28:57,220
Mutual affection is a great joy.

367
00:29:07,800 --> 00:29:09,470
Wishing you prosperity, sir.

368
00:29:10,630 --> 00:29:12,430
What song would you like to hear?

369
00:29:12,630 --> 00:29:14,030
"Ambush from All Sides."

370
00:29:23,830 --> 00:29:24,700
Quite fitting.

371
00:30:27,740 --> 00:30:31,670
I didn't know you could play that song
on a three-stringed instrument.

372
00:31:31,590 --> 00:31:32,780
Quite a turnout.

373
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:35,840
Just wait to collect the bodies.

374
00:31:53,350 --> 00:31:55,110
Where are you going, Auntie?

375
00:31:57,540 --> 00:31:59,220
Are you the boss or am I?

376
00:32:39,210 --> 00:32:40,210
Twelve in total—

377
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:42,770
don't leave anyone behind.

378
00:32:53,110 --> 00:32:54,110
Don't be nervous.

379
00:32:54,950 --> 00:32:56,300
The best is yet to come.

380
00:32:57,660 --> 00:32:58,350
Attack!

381
00:33:03,260 --> 00:33:03,870
General.

382
00:33:11,110 --> 00:33:12,600
Before you go looking for trouble,

383
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:13,920
think about how many lives you have.

384
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:14,560
Move!

385
00:33:23,210 --> 00:33:24,010
Inspector Su.

386
00:33:25,550 --> 00:33:27,350
This is a day worth celebrating.

387
00:34:46,350 --> 00:34:47,639
How could you lie to me?

388
00:34:49,199 --> 00:34:52,760
I was going to save you for last.

389
00:35:16,720 --> 00:35:18,390
Put them all in the truck ahead.

390
00:35:18,390 --> 00:35:18,990
Move!

391
00:35:24,920 --> 00:35:25,650
Director Li.

392
00:35:28,020 --> 00:35:30,330
That was a beautiful fight.

393
00:35:39,960 --> 00:35:41,420
Life really is like a play.

394
00:35:42,080 --> 00:35:44,480
It all comes down to
who's the better actor.

395
00:35:48,520 --> 00:35:50,040
You're the expert.

396
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:52,650
Your acting skills are excellent.

397
00:36:27,190 --> 00:36:28,110
It's Auntie.

398
00:36:28,710 --> 00:36:29,630
It's Auntie!

399
00:36:30,300 --> 00:36:31,190
Auntie!

400
00:36:31,820 --> 00:36:32,820
Auntie!

401
00:36:33,460 --> 00:36:34,390
Auntie!

402
00:36:36,110 --> 00:36:37,380
Let go of me!

403
00:36:45,520 --> 00:36:46,640
Let go of me!

404
00:36:48,340 --> 00:36:49,750
It's Auntie!

405
00:36:58,630 --> 00:36:59,760
Did you bring an axe?

406
00:37:00,860 --> 00:37:02,520
If you have to, just cut it off.

407
00:37:03,240 --> 00:37:04,010
Got it.

408
00:37:11,820 --> 00:37:12,820
Du Huangqiao!

409
00:37:13,100 --> 00:37:14,410
You bastard!

410
00:37:14,530 --> 00:37:15,840
I'll kill you!

411
00:37:17,270 --> 00:37:18,630
You're from No. 76.

412
00:37:24,110 --> 00:37:26,710
Didn't you say you wanted to
save this country?

413
00:37:45,600 --> 00:37:46,930
So you're Cleaner?

414
00:37:47,300 --> 00:37:49,050
You scared the hell out of me.

415
00:37:51,210 --> 00:37:52,970
It couldn't be that bad, Mr. Zhao.

416
00:37:52,970 --> 00:37:54,230
I'll be counting on you

417
00:37:55,390 --> 00:37:57,030
to look out for me from now on.

418
00:37:57,450 --> 00:37:58,810
Me, look out for you?

419
00:37:59,160 --> 00:38:01,600
From now on, I'd better
learn how to tell fortunes too.

420
00:38:01,600 --> 00:38:02,450
In this world,

421
00:38:02,680 --> 00:38:04,480
the blind are the most ruthless.

422
00:38:15,680 --> 00:38:16,450
Fall in!

423
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:03,850
Get some rest early.

424
00:39:06,370 --> 00:39:07,770
I want to make more money.

425
00:39:08,810 --> 00:39:09,480
What?

426
00:39:10,850 --> 00:39:12,290
Lots and lots of money.

427
00:39:17,500 --> 00:39:19,760
What's the point of making so much money?

428
00:39:23,850 --> 00:39:25,250
Once we've saved enough,

429
00:39:27,290 --> 00:39:28,890
let's move back to Hangzhou.

430
00:39:31,810 --> 00:39:34,040
I don't want to end up like Auntie,

431
00:39:36,410 --> 00:39:38,670
leaving behind nothing but a cloth shoe.

432
00:39:42,810 --> 00:39:44,290
I just can't make it out—

433
00:39:45,410 --> 00:39:47,720
how could Auntie have been from the NBIS?

434
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:53,640
Does everyone have secrets?

435
00:39:58,970 --> 00:39:59,890
Chen.

436
00:40:03,500 --> 00:40:05,560
Are you hiding something from me too?

437
00:40:06,470 --> 00:40:07,960
Auntie was from the NBIS,

438
00:40:10,810 --> 00:40:12,470
and Du Huangqiao is a traitor.

439
00:40:16,490 --> 00:40:17,640
Then what are you?

440
00:40:20,160 --> 00:40:21,330
Tell me the truth.

441
00:40:21,980 --> 00:40:24,460
I... I'm a photographer.

442
00:40:27,420 --> 00:40:28,420
No. That's not it.

443
00:40:30,680 --> 00:40:32,560
You've been going to Fairy Bath
for no reason

444
00:40:32,560 --> 00:40:33,690
these past few days.

445
00:40:36,970 --> 00:40:38,770
What exactly have you been up to?

446
00:40:46,850 --> 00:40:48,200
I went to see my cousin.

447
00:40:53,290 --> 00:40:54,560
She was at Fairy Bath?

448
00:40:55,450 --> 00:40:58,160
Du Huangqiao disguised himself
as a Communist,

449
00:40:59,160 --> 00:41:00,820
broke her out of the hospital,

450
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:03,640
and hid her in the bathhouse.

451
00:41:06,370 --> 00:41:07,900
Why didn't you tell me about

452
00:41:09,080 --> 00:41:10,480
something this serious?

453
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:13,960
The more people who know,
the greater the danger.

454
00:41:13,960 --> 00:41:15,490
I didn't want to drag you into this.

455
00:41:15,490 --> 00:41:16,370
Nonsense.

456
00:41:17,680 --> 00:41:19,080
You just don't trust me.

457
00:41:24,600 --> 00:41:28,000
That blind bastard really had you
wrapped around his finger.

458
00:41:33,370 --> 00:41:34,770
Where's your cousin now?

459
00:41:37,080 --> 00:41:38,410
That blind bastard said

460
00:41:38,680 --> 00:41:39,940
she was sent to Yan'an.

461
00:41:44,120 --> 00:41:46,280
More like she was sent to hell.

462
00:41:48,560 --> 00:41:49,370
Impossible.

463
00:41:51,040 --> 00:41:52,840
My cousin's smart and vigilant.

464
00:41:53,080 --> 00:41:54,610
She must've found a way out.

465
00:41:57,290 --> 00:41:58,520
Wasn't Auntie smart?

466
00:41:58,710 --> 00:41:59,910
Wasn't she vigilant?

467
00:42:02,130 --> 00:42:05,460
She was even so nice to that blind bastard
when she was alive.

468
00:42:07,240 --> 00:42:10,300
And in the end, she didn't even
have an intact body left.

469
00:42:16,730 --> 00:42:17,560
Chen.

470
00:42:20,450 --> 00:42:21,510
You must promise me

471
00:42:23,010 --> 00:42:25,940
that from now on, you'll never
keep anything from me.

472
00:42:31,770 --> 00:42:33,570
We have to stay alive, both of us.

473
00:42:36,370 --> 00:42:38,170
We came from Hangzhou together,

474
00:42:40,810 --> 00:42:42,340
and when it's time to leave,

475
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:46,080
we'll leave together.

476
00:42:53,860 --> 00:42:54,610
Okay.
